			"widgets_values":[
				"How the reference pictures align with the target video — Picture 1 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 0.00-second mark of the target video; Picture 2 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 5.00-second mark of the target video; Picture 3 provides the exact character identity, costume design, hairstyle, body proportions, and staff weapon reference that must remain consistent throughout the shot.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description:\n[Shot 1] One continuous five-second cinematic fantasy martial-arts shot. Begin exactly from <Picture 1>. Preserve the same adult female martial heroine established by <Picture 1> and <Picture 3>: the same face, hairstyle with twin buns, green-black outfit, translucent flowing sleeves and ribbons, thigh tattoo, long ornate staff, body proportions, and elegant yet combat-ready temperament. Also preserve the same large turquoise Chinese dragon with gold whiskers and antler-like horns, along with the high-altitude cloudscape, towering cliffs, and distant ancient pagodas in the opening frame.\n\nAt the start of the shot, the heroine is riding the flying dragon in the same composition and pose established by <Picture 1>. Her hair ribbons, sleeves, and waist ornaments flow naturally in the strong wind, while the dragon moves powerfully through the sky with a serpentine body motion. The dragon immediately surges forward and slightly downward through the clouds, creating a sense of acceleration and momentum. The heroine adjusts her balance on the dragon’s back while keeping firm control of the staff.\n\nAs the motion builds, the dragon performs a strong sweeping dive through the cloud corridor toward the battlefield below. Using this momentum, the heroine launches herself cleanly off the dragon in one fluid action. She pushes off from the dragon’s back, enters a dynamic aerial descent, and rotates her torso while bringing the staff into a ready striking position. Her movement must feel physically coherent and elegant: dragon dive → leap from the dragon → airborne descent → staff rotation into attack. Do not introduce unrelated flips, teleportation, extra weapons, or abrupt pose changes.\n\nDuring the descent, the environment transitions naturally from the cloud kingdom into the battle setting of <Picture 2>. Ancient East Asian architecture, stormy dramatic skies, scattered debris, and multiple hostile enemies progressively come into view. The heroine’s trailing ribbons and sleeves create strong flowing arcs around her body, emphasizing speed and grace. Her staff should remain rigid, clearly readable, and consistently designed according to <Picture 3>.\n\nIn the latter half of the shot, she completes the aerial approach and lands into a forceful sweeping strike. She plants her footing with a wide martial stance and drives the long staff across the frame in a powerful horizontal or slightly diagonal attack. The action must feel like one continuous finishing move that converts the dragon-assisted aerial entry into a decisive battlefield strike. One enemy is lifted or knocked upward by the impact, matching the airborne opponent seen in <Picture 2>, while surrounding enemies remain active in the background.\n\nProgressively converge toward <Picture 2> during the final phase. The heroine must settle into the same dominant combat pose and composition seen in the final frame: staff extended across the frame, legs spread in a strong grounded stance, torso turned with controlled power, ribbons and sleeves streaming outward, and one enemy figure airborne in the upper-right area. The battlefield should be crowded and energetic, with traditional buildings, debris, and combat activity in the background under a dramatic sky.\n\nAt the 5.00-second mark, land precisely on <Picture 2>: the heroine is in the exact finishing attack pose and framing of the reference, using the long staff in a wide sweeping strike, with the airborne enemy, surrounding warriors, architectural environment, dramatic clouds, motion intensity, and composition closely matching <Picture 2>.\n\nUse one continuous shot with no cuts. The camera begins with a majestic fantasy framing on the flying dragon, then performs a smooth forward and slightly descending tracking move that follows the heroine into the battlefield. The camera may subtly widen and lower as she leaves the dragon and enters combat, but it must remain cinematic and controlled. Do not use abrupt zooms, chaotic shaking, or excessive orbiting. The transition from <Picture 1> to <Picture 2> should be driven mainly by the heroine’s movement and the dragon’s dive momentum.\n\nMaintain stable facial identity, stable anatomy, clean hands, coherent limb motion, consistent costume details, stable staff design, natural cloth and ribbon dynamics, consistent dragon anatomy, and smooth environmental continuity. Preserve a polished fantasy illustration look with strong readability, dramatic lighting, and natural directional motion blur only during the fastest movement.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nPowerful wind rushing through the clouds, subtle dragon flight movement, fluttering cloth and ribbons, one strong leap-off accent, fast descending air movement, clean staff swing whooshes, impact debris, and a sharp combat hit synchronized with the final sweeping strike that launches the enemy upward. Keep the ambience stable and cinematic, with no clipping, hiss, or distortion.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A",
